        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_987562195.1",
        "comments": "The assembly bTacRuf1.hap1.1 is based on 54x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. MicroFinder was used to order scaffolds prior to curation. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The curated assembly has a diploid chromosome number of 2n = 72, based on the Hi-C contact map. This differs from the published karyotype for Tachybaptus ruficollis, which reports a diploid chromosome number of 2n = 60 (Patawang et al., 2022). Z chromosome identified by synteny analysis with Anas platyrhynchos (GCA_964188345.1) The exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on are uncertain on: Chromosome 1 (87,660 ? 89,782 Kbp), Chromosome 2 (65,398 ? 66,958 Kbp), Chromosome 3 (38,069 ? 47,554 Kbp), Chromosome 5 (23,387 ? 24,730 Kbp), Chromosome 8 (26,246 ? 27,112 & 31,356 ? 33,435 Kbp), Chromosome 11 (2,468 ? 7,665 Kbp), Chromosome 15 (2,685 ? 4,504 kbp), Chromosome 23 (1 ? 2,078 Kbp), Chromosome 26 (1,256 ? 2,598 Kbp) & Chromosome 27 (2,901 ? 3,727 Kbp).",
